{"id": "EUVD-2026-102496", "enisaUuid": "f2909330-0d54-3150-b970-f1b202081a81", "description": "ThinkCMF through 8.0.1 contains an incorrect authorization vulnerability in RestAdminBaseController that allows restricted backend administrators to call every admin REST API endpoint because Auth::check() fails open when no admin_api rule exists. Attackers with a valid admin-type API token can list member emails and mobile numbers, disable members, and call PUT admin/roles/{id}/authorize to grant themselves full administrator rights.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T21:43:42", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/thinkcmf-admin-rest-api-missing-authorization", "https://github.com/thinkcmf/cmf-core/blob/v8.0.3/src/lib/Auth.php#L40-L61", "https://github.com/thinkcmf/cmf-core/blob/v8.0.3/src/controller/RestAdminBaseController.php#L15-L34", "https://github.com/thinkcmf/cmf-api/blob/v8.0.7/src/admin/controller/RoleController.php#L345-L381", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/thinkcmf-through-8.0.1-incorrect-authorization-in-admin-rest-api"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111352", "GHSA-qf7c-pg8v-q3rx"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.36, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e01ddddf-a72a-30bb-af31-fa1233c5cdcc", "product": {"name": "ThinkCMF", "vendor": {"name": "Naichen"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22648.0.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2b754404-1e19-3f65-85d2-68441bc49c6e", "vendor": {"name": "ThinkCMF"}}], "isExploited": false}